1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,700
(EP03 Behind-the-Scenes)

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:05,980
(Behind-the-Scenes 1)

3
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:08,060
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Pass out the bowls and chopsticks.

4
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:14,100
Then bring over some stools.

5
00:00:17,310 --> 00:00:18,670
We'll sit down first.

6
00:00:18,670 --> 00:00:19,300
Okay.

7
00:00:20,590 --> 00:00:21,820
Sorry about that.

8
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:23,700
You can put this in here.

9
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:24,980
They're supposed to go together.

10
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:28,990
We'll start digging in.

11
00:00:29,470 --> 00:00:30,270
Go on.

12
00:00:30,870 --> 00:00:31,670
Let's eat together.

13
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:33,700
We served way too many bowls.

14
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:35,980
I just want a small portion.

15
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:37,740
(Pointing)

16
00:00:38,230 --> 00:00:40,190
Today is going
to be the fullest I've eaten.

17
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:41,990
Definitely.

18
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:45,620
My motto today is to eat my fill.

19
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:46,420
Eat my fill.

20
00:00:47,670 --> 00:00:48,700
"The King of Eating".

21
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:51,030
You're the "King of Eating" today.

22
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:52,340
(Glances)

23
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:53,620
That's me.

24
00:00:57,820 --> 00:00:59,260
(Glances)

25
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:04,700
(Standing up)

26
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:07,820
(Moving closer to take a photo)

27
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:11,710
You look so good cooking.

28
00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:14,620
This shot looks great, Yang.

29
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:15,740
(Satisfied)

30
00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:19,620
I'm really
looking forward to his shrimp.

31
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:22,030
A guy who can cook is such a catch.

32
00:01:22,630 --> 00:01:24,310
Your skewers look pretty good too.

33
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:29,340
You're too kind.

34
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:34,340
(Behind-the-Scenes 2)

35
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:35,569
(Behind-the-Scenes)

36
00:01:35,569 --> 00:01:36,940
(Stargazing room)

37
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:38,640
So you're more of a Judging type?

38
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:39,400
Judging personality type?

39
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:40,500
Not really, actually.

40
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:41,540
I'm more of a Perceiving type.

41
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:44,140
I kind of wish

42
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:45,220
I were a Judging type.

43
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:46,860
Yeah. Good at making plans, right?

44
00:01:48,070 --> 00:01:49,670
(Asking)
What do you think I am?

45
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,100
(Thinking seriously)

46
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:58,150
ISTJ (Logistician).

47
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:02,340
You're wrong.

48
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:04,180
Then what are you?

49
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:04,710
Tell me.

50
00:02:05,030 --> 00:02:06,590
I honestly can't even tell
those letters apart.

51
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:08,380
Okay.

52
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:09,620
INTJ (Architect).

53
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:10,180
Oh, INTJ (Architect).

54
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:11,540
So what's the difference

55
00:02:11,540 --> 00:02:12,590
between S (Sensing) and N (Intuitive)?

56
00:02:14,070 --> 00:02:16,110
I guess I just like thinking.

57
00:02:16,110 --> 00:02:16,980
I like imagining things.

58
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:17,630
Imagining things?

59
00:02:17,630 --> 00:02:18,220
Yeah.

60
00:02:18,830 --> 00:02:19,940
You don't like imagining things?

61
00:02:19,940 --> 00:02:21,860
I love imagining things.

62
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:23,260
(Amused)

63
00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:26,430
What do you imagine?

64
00:02:26,430 --> 00:02:27,950
All kinds of things.

65
00:02:27,950 --> 00:02:28,550
Tell me about it.

66
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:30,380
Sometimes I just zone out.

67
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:32,620
I'll stare blankly at one spot.

68
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:33,740
And that's when I start

69
00:02:33,740 --> 00:02:34,700
imagining things.

70
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:35,540
I think about all kinds of things.

71
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:36,700
Do you do that too?

72
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:37,020
Yeah.

73
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:38,620
I like zoning out too.

74
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:47,980
(Behind-the-Scenes 3)

75
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:51,020
(Behind-the-Scenes)

76
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:52,550
Do you usually cook at home?

77
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:53,660
(Curious)

78
00:02:55,180 --> 00:02:56,020
Not very often.

79
00:02:57,420 --> 00:02:59,420
I use the air fryer sometimes.

80
00:03:00,710 --> 00:03:01,750
Just simple stuff.

81
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:05,900
What are you good at making?

82
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:06,820
I don't know.

83
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:07,780
This is only my third time cooking.

84
00:03:08,850 --> 00:03:09,850
(Surprised)
Your third time cooking?

85
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:11,670
My third time in the past two years.

86
00:03:12,510 --> 00:03:14,230
So you don't really cook much either.

87
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:15,900
Right. Yesterday was my second time.

88
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:18,260
(Asking)
How long did your shrimp take yesterday?

89
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:22,110
About 30 or 40 minutes.

90
00:03:22,750 --> 00:03:24,550
That's quite a project.

91
00:03:25,470 --> 00:03:26,830
Mostly because I had to thaw them first.

92
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:28,100
Live shrimp are easier.

93
00:03:30,430 --> 00:03:32,670
So did you come up
with that recipe yourself?

94
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:35,860
I just winged it yesterday.

95
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:37,980
I used to make it a lot
when I was little.

96
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:40,790
Being here reminded me how to make it.

97
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:42,780
I think you might have a knack for it.

98
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:43,500
What?

99
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:44,900
(Listening intently)
I think you're pretty talented.

100
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:46,100
That's impressive.

101
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:47,260
You're really good at it.

102
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:58,700
(Behind-the-Scenes 4)

103
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:01,020
(Behind-the-Scenes.
Washing dishes together)

104
00:04:02,190 --> 00:04:03,750
Look at your egg yolk.

105
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:05,900
You can pull this out.

106
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:07,660
Rinse it off.

107
00:04:09,710 --> 00:04:10,670
Why is it so hard?

108
00:04:12,230 --> 00:04:13,030
It's okay.

109
00:04:13,750 --> 00:04:14,580
Here.

110
00:04:18,830 --> 00:04:20,350
A little higher.

111
00:04:22,620 --> 00:04:23,260
Put it back.

112
00:04:24,260 --> 00:04:25,380
Okay, put it back.

113
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:33,310
This bowl's about to hit the other one.

114
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:38,460
You can use that big plate.

115
00:04:38,630 --> 00:04:39,830
This is for fruit.

116
00:04:39,830 --> 00:04:40,540
This?

117
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:41,140
Yeah.

118
00:04:41,140 --> 00:04:42,830
Then hurry and wash it
so they can use it.

119
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,460
(Obeying)

120
00:04:49,030 --> 00:04:49,870
You can put fruit in now.

121
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:50,670
For fruit.

122
00:04:51,350 --> 00:04:52,310
Okay, thanks.

123
00:04:53,670 --> 00:04:53,940
Wait.

124
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:55,380
I just felt something really big.

125
00:04:57,540 --> 00:04:58,060
An onion.

126
00:05:00,470 --> 00:05:02,630
It ran out of water
right after I took it out.

127
00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:05,470
It really did.

128
00:05:07,350 --> 00:05:08,830
This is cracking me up.

129
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:15,180
(Behind-the-Scenes 5)

130
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:16,740
(Behind-the-Scenes)

131
00:05:16,740 --> 00:05:17,990
Have you been busy lately?

132
00:05:18,230 --> 00:05:20,030
Actually,

133
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:20,750
not really.

134
00:05:20,750 --> 00:05:23,550
It's not one
of those super busy periods.

135
00:05:23,860 --> 00:05:26,860
I feel like coming to Signal House
is a chance to relax.

136
00:05:28,470 --> 00:05:29,630
You're here to have fun, right?

137
00:05:29,630 --> 00:05:31,060
Yeah.

138
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:31,990
Of course.

139
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:35,300
You fell into my trap again.

140
00:05:36,390 --> 00:05:37,060
All kinds of traps.

141
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:37,700
Yeah, all kinds of traps.

142
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:38,310
All these little traps.

143
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:39,150
I'm being so sincere.

144
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:41,140
I'm sincere too.

145
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:42,620
Really?

146
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:45,180
Then tell me, am I sincere?

147
00:05:45,310 --> 00:05:46,310
(Blurting it out)
You're sincere.

148
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:51,580
I'm actually... How should I put it?

149
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:52,820
I'm pretty slow to warm up.

150
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:53,860
What do you think?

151
00:05:55,870 --> 00:05:56,950
I'm pretty slow to warm up too.

152
00:05:56,950 --> 00:05:57,620
Have you noticed?

153
00:05:58,390 --> 00:05:59,180
You really...

154
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:01,350
Why are you laughing now?

155
00:06:01,350 --> 00:06:02,860
Yeah, I just...

156
00:06:02,860 --> 00:06:04,820
I feel like laughing
when I'm happy. Okay?

157
00:06:05,230 --> 00:06:05,660
Okay.

158
00:06:06,390 --> 00:06:07,430
What if I get nervous?

159
00:06:07,830 --> 00:06:08,710
Nervous about what?

160
00:06:08,710 --> 00:06:10,420
Come on, paddle a little.

161
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:11,220
Okay, paddle a little.

162
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:12,540
A little.

163
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:13,780
Relax.

164
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:16,660
I think while you're doing
something else,

165
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:17,230
you will...

166
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:23,220
When you're paddling,
you might say a lot of things

167
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:25,500
without even realizing it.

168
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:27,510
It's when you're being the most genuine.

169
00:06:27,510 --> 00:06:28,750
And you said
you weren't good at talking.

170
00:06:28,750 --> 00:06:29,630
You actually do.

171
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:31,580
You're better at it than me.

172
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:34,420
I'm com...

173
00:06:34,660 --> 00:06:35,500
Complimenting you.

174
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:36,430
I am complimenting you.

175
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:37,390
Thanks.

176
00:06:39,620 --> 00:06:44,580
(Behind-the-Scenes 6)

177
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:46,390
(Behind-the-Scenes)
I want to arrange these flowers.

178
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:51,260
I really love buying flowers.

179
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:53,820
But I usually get them
at a flower market.

180
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:55,790
Then I thought,

181
00:06:55,910 --> 00:06:58,430
since it's Children's Day,

182
00:06:58,430 --> 00:06:59,790
I'd buy some for everyone.

183
00:06:59,950 --> 00:07:01,110
Thank you.

184
00:07:02,220 --> 00:07:03,220
I'm going to change.

185
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:04,030
Okay.

186
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:07,700
Have you ever imagined

187
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:09,150
what your wedding bouquet
would look like?

188
00:07:09,150 --> 00:07:10,670
I've never thought about it.

189
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:11,500
(Just kidding)

190
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:12,700
That's actually hilarious.

191
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:15,180
I'd choose calla lilies.

192
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:18,540
(Focused)

193
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:20,340
Why are they... Is it too warm?

194
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:21,500
They're all about to bloom.

195
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:22,770
Oh my gosh.

196
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:23,980
Oh my.

197
00:07:23,980 --> 00:07:26,340
Is it because you're holding them
and warming them up?

198
00:07:26,630 --> 00:07:27,630
You know,

199
00:07:27,630 --> 00:07:28,900
if you keep them in winter,

200
00:07:28,900 --> 00:07:29,860
and it's too warm,

201
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:30,940
they'll all burst open.

202
00:07:31,710 --> 00:07:32,600
But it's summer now,

203
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,580
so they're definitely going
to burst open.

204
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:34,430
Actually, look.

205
00:07:34,830 --> 00:07:36,390
They're all ready to open.

206
00:07:36,390 --> 00:07:37,580
(They're all ready to open)

207
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:39,110
I've come to terms with it.

208
00:07:39,430 --> 00:07:40,820
That's really how it is.

209
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:42,020
They're really opening up.

210
00:07:43,540 --> 00:07:44,620
That's hilarious.

211
00:07:44,660 --> 00:07:49,620
(Behind-the-Scenes 7)

212
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:51,620
(Behind-the-Scenes)

213
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:54,270
You seem much happier these days.

214
00:07:54,270 --> 00:07:55,190
Why?

215
00:07:59,590 --> 00:08:00,870
The other side of Cao Yiheng. Why?

216
00:08:03,390 --> 00:08:05,030
Because seeing you
always makes me happy.

217
00:08:05,030 --> 00:08:05,820
(Glances)

218
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:07,580
(Laughs)

219
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:09,860
I'm really happy to see you.

220
00:08:11,630 --> 00:08:13,270
And then you start talking more?

221
00:08:13,270 --> 00:08:13,830
Yeah.

222
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:19,620
If I don't start conversations,

223
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:21,990
people will assume

224
00:08:22,540 --> 00:08:23,300
I'm upset.

225
00:08:23,950 --> 00:08:25,190
I don't feel that way.

226
00:08:25,460 --> 00:08:27,220
(Glances)

227
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:28,590
You don't think I'm unhappy?

228
00:08:28,590 --> 00:08:30,870
No, I don't think you're unhappy.

229
00:08:31,830 --> 00:08:33,950
I just feel like
you get a little awkward.

230
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:37,540
I'm just afraid
I'll give people the wrong idea.

231
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:46,140
Do you feel like talking too much

232
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:47,180
would affect you at all?

233
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:48,420
Or

234
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:49,710
would it be

235
00:08:49,710 --> 00:08:51,110
hard for you to keep up?

236
00:08:52,220 --> 00:08:53,100
I don't think so.

237
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:54,750
I'm pretty good at keeping up.

238
00:08:56,540 --> 00:09:00,180
So you're usually this quiet,

239
00:09:00,310 --> 00:09:03,230
but you talk a little more
when you're dating?

240
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:04,780
Yeah.

241
00:09:05,430 --> 00:09:08,310
I'm more focused
and selective about who I talk to.

242
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:10,020
Hurry up and draw.

243
00:09:15,540 --> 00:09:20,500
(Behind-the-Scenes 8)

244
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:21,380
(Behind-the-Scenes)

245
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:23,020
Do you play the piano?

246
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:24,140
Can I hear you play?

247
00:09:24,550 --> 00:09:25,910
I'll play a little something for you.

248
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:28,300
Half a song. I only know half of it.

249
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:29,020
What song?

250
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:29,700
Just listen.

251
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:30,860
Maybe you've heard it before.

252
00:09:36,540 --> 00:09:37,540
You're too humble.

253
00:09:37,540 --> 00:09:38,180
(Praise)

254
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:41,300
That's marvelous.

255
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:41,700
You know?

256
00:09:43,460 --> 00:09:46,300
(Listening intently)

257
00:10:01,110 --> 00:10:02,470
That's all I remember.

258
00:10:02,470 --> 00:10:03,590
Marvelous.

259
00:10:03,590 --> 00:10:04,020
(Keep praising)

260
00:10:04,060 --> 00:10:05,180
(Teasing)
Splendid.

261
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:07,460
That's just outstanding.

262
00:10:07,460 --> 00:10:09,710
Were you thinking of what to say?

263
00:10:10,390 --> 00:10:11,100
It was really good.

264
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:12,110
Thanks.

265
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:18,540
(Behind-the-Scenes 9)

266
00:10:18,870 --> 00:10:20,870
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Independent, or do you rely on friends?

267
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:21,790
Neither, really.

268
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:23,470
I rarely do things

269
00:10:23,470 --> 00:10:24,470
completely on my own.

270
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:26,940
(Curious)
Do you ever rebel?

271
00:10:27,020 --> 00:10:28,020
Sometimes.

272
00:10:28,860 --> 00:10:30,310
What about you? Do you rebel?

273
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:32,460
(Glances)

274
00:10:32,670 --> 00:10:34,060
Not often. Almost never.

275
00:10:34,060 --> 00:10:35,820
You can figure some things out yourself.

276
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:36,820
So there's no need to rebel.

277
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:39,820
You're pretty mature, then.

278
00:10:41,270 --> 00:10:42,350
Do you feel like

279
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:44,190
you still haven't fully opened up?

280
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:44,980
Me?

281
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:47,940
I'm more comfortable around guys.

282
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:49,140
That's normal.

283
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:52,180
But with girls, I can be a little...

284
00:10:54,180 --> 00:10:55,460
A little shy.

285
00:11:00,830 --> 00:11:02,270
